From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:43:59 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: store an immediate through a scratch register

A64 has no store of an immediate, so an assignment of a constant to
memory or to a stack array, such as `buf[i] = 0x80;`, remained after
lowering and was rejected at linearization. Lowering now moves the
constant to a fresh 64-bit scratch variable and stores its low bytes
with STR, STRH or STRB.

The lowering proof shows that the scratch variable, which the program
cannot name, is the only state the first instruction changes, and that
the store writes the bytes of the source assignment.
---
 compiler/tests/success/armv8a/store_imm.jazz | 19 +++++++
 proofs/compiler/armv8a_lowering.v            | 33 +++++++++--
 proofs/compiler/armv8a_lowering_proof.v      | 59 ++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 compiler/tests/success/armv8a/store_imm.jazz

diff --git a/compiler/tests/success/armv8a/store_imm.jazz b/compiler/tests/success/armv8a/store_imm.jazz
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..c3751f9fc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/compiler/tests/success/armv8a/store_imm.jazz
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+/* A64 has no store of an immediate: a constant stored to memory or to a
+   stack array goes through a scratch register, for every access size. */
+export fn store_imm(reg u64 p i) -> reg u64 {
+  stack u8[16] buf;
+  reg u64 r;
+  inline int j;
+
+  for j = 0 to 16 { buf[j] = 0; }
+
+  i &= 15;
+  buf[i] = 0x80;
+  [:u8 p + i] = 0x80;
+  [:u16 p + 2] = 0xbeef;
+  [:u32 p + 4] = 0;
+  [:u64 p + 8] = 0x0123456789abcdef;
+
+  r = (64u) buf[0];
+  return r;
+}
